sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: To find two rational straight lines commensurable in square only such that the square on the greater is greater than the square on the less by the square on a straight line incommensurable in length with the greater.
----
proof:

Set out a rational straight line {AB}, and two square numbers {CE} and {ED|DE} such that their sum {CD} is not square. Describe the semicircle {AFB|semih} on {AB}. Let it be contrived that {DC|CD} is to {CE} as the square on {BA|AB} is to the square on {AF}, and join {FB}. <div class="just"><a href="/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX29/#lemma2">X.29.Lem.2</a><br><a href="/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX6/#cor">X.6,Cor.</a></div>

Then, in a similar manner to the preceding, we can prove that {BA|AB} and {AF} are rational straight lines commensurable in square only.

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="280" height="200" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="X.30 diagram" src="propX30.gif"/></noscript>
